---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who's behind CommunitySolarPA, why it exists, where our information comes from, and how to reach us."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <div class="eyebrow">Our mission</div>
      <h1>Helping Pennsylvania adopt solar, for everyone</h1>
      <p>
        We're working to help Pennsylvania adopt solar energy at scale. We believe community solar
        can deliver three things at once:
      </p>
      <div class="grid" style="margin:1.5em 0">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A cleaner future</h3>
          <p>Power from the sun instead of burning fossil fuels.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Lasting energy independence</h3>
          <p>Energy produced here in Pennsylvania, from a source that never runs out.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Solar for everyone</h3>
          <p>Renters, apartment dwellers, and households on every budget can benefit, not just homeowners with a sunny roof.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Explain community solar</strong> in plain language, so Pennsylvanians know what it is and how it works.</li>
        <li><strong>Track Pennsylvania's progress</strong> on the legislation and rules that would make it possible.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep people informed</strong> when there's news and when community solar becomes available in their area.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who's behind this</h2>
      <p>
        CommunitySolarPA was started by a Philadelphia resident who has lived in other states and wants to
        help bring community solar to life in Pennsylvania. The goal is simple: more clean, environmentally
        friendly energy produced here at home, and lower energy bills for everyone, whether they own, rent,
        or have never had a roof of their own to put panels on.
      </p>
      <p>
        CommunitySolarPA is an independent information project. We don't sell solar, we don't take money from
        solar companies, and we never sell or share the information people give us. See our
        <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where our information comes from</h2>
      <p>We build every page from public sources and link to them on the page, so you can check our work:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The bill itself.</strong> What we say about Pennsylvania's community solar bill comes from the text of HB 504 as passed by the State House, published by the <a href="https://www.palegis.us/legislation/bills/2025/hb504" rel="noopener">Pennsylvania General Assembly</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Utilities and prices.</strong> Prices to compare come from <a href="https://www.papowerswitch.com/" rel="noopener">PA PowerSwitch</a>, run by the Pennsylvania Public Utility Commission. Which utility serves each ZIP code comes from U.S. Department of Energy data.</li>
        <li><strong>County numbers.</strong> Figures on renters, rowhomes, apartments and mobile homes come from the U.S. Census Bureau's American Community Survey.</li>
        <li><strong>Other states.</strong> Program details come from state agencies, program websites, and reporting we cite on each page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Rules and prices change, and we're not lawyers or financial advisors. If you spot something that's out of
        date or wrong, please tell us and we'll fix it.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, ideas, or want to help? Email
        <a href="mailto:chris@communitysolarpa.org">chris@communitysolarpa.org</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Signup />
</Base>
